      "name": "ActivateInventoryPanelStateCallback",
      "signature": "int ActivateInventoryPanelStateCallback(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Callback that activates the inventory panel state by setting bit 1.\n\nClassification: Callback/Handler - Used as sub-panel callback (_g_pfnSubPanelCallback).\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load g_pInventoryPanelState global pointer\n2. Call SetOrClearBitMask with bit value 1 to set the active bit\n3. Return 1 to indicate success\n\nParameters: None (callback signature)\n\nReturns:\n- 1: Always returns success\n\nCallers: Referenced as callback from FUN_6fa03a80, FUN_6fa05010, FUN_6fa04c10 via\n         function pointer assignment to _g_pfnSubPanelCallback.\n\nCalled Functions:\n- SetOrClearBitMask(g_pInventoryPanelState, 1): Sets bit 1 on the panel state\n\nGlobal Data:\n- g_pInventoryPanelState (0x6fa21788): Pointer to inventory panel state structure",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.08",
