      "name": "GetGameListDataPointer",
      "signature": "int GetGameListDataPointer(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Returns pointer to global game list data structure (g_pGameListData).\n\nWARNING: Function boundary incorrect in Ghidra. Actual function spans 0x6fa04250-0x6fa0426e\n(31 bytes) but Ghidra shows only 1 instruction. Full disassembly from raw bytes:\n\n  6fa04250: MOV EAX, [0x6fa21728]    ; Load g_pGameListData\n  6fa04255: MOV CL, [EAX+0x225]      ; Check connection status byte\n  6fa0425b: TEST CL, CL\n  6fa0425d: JZ 6fa0426c              ; If not connected, return 0\n  6fa0425f: CALL 6fa1288e            ; Validate connection\n  6fa04264: TEST EAX, EAX\n  6fa04266: JNZ 6fa0426c             ; If valid, return 0\n  6fa04268: OR EAX, -1               ; Set EAX = -1\n  6fa0426b: RET                      ; Return -1 (invalid connection)\n  6fa0426c: XOR EAX, EAX             ; Set EAX = 0\n  6fa0426e: RET                      ; Return 0 (success or not connected)\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load g_pGameListData global pointer into EAX\n2. Check byte at offset +0x225 (connection status flag)\n3. If zero (not connected), return 0\n4. If non-zero, call connection validation function at 0x6fa1288e\n5. If validation succeeds (returns non-zero), return 0\n6. If validation fails (returns zero), return -1\n\nParameters: None\n\nReturns:\n  0  - Success (either not connected or connection valid)\n  -1 - Connection exists but validation failed\n\nCallers check return value == -1 to detect invalid connection state.",
