      "name": "InitializeBattleNetSession",
      "signature": "int InitializeBattleNetSession(void * pGameListData)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Initializes and enters the Battle.net multiplayer session.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Store pGameListData pointer in g_pGameListData global for access by other functions\n2. Initialize pentagram UI resources (loading screen graphics)\n3. Initialize application display with parameter 1 (enable display mode)\n4. Enter the main Battle.net multiplayer UI loop via EnterBattleNetMultiplayerUI\n5. Release inventory pool resources after UI session ends\n6. Return current sub-panel state from g_nSubPanelState\n\nParameters:\n  pGameListData (ECX) - Pointer to game list data structure containing:\n    +0x1ea: ushort flags (control bits for UI mode)\n    +0x21d: Callback vtable pointer\n    +0x356: Character slot state byte\n    +0x359: Connection info offset\n\nReturns:\n  int - Sub-panel state value from g_nSubPanelState indicating session result:\n    0 = Normal exit\n    4 = Error/cleanup state\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Function is called via function pointer table at 0x6fa1dae4\n  - Acts as wrapper/entry point for Battle.net multiplayer initialization\n  - EnterBattleNetMultiplayerUI handles the main event loop and all cleanup\n\nClassification: Initialization wrapper",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.08",
