      "name": "CancelSubPanelAndStopMessageLoop",
      "signature": "int CancelSubPanelAndStopMessageLoop(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Callback function to cancel sub-panel UI and stop message loop processing.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Set g_nSubPanelState = 4 (cancelled/closed state)\n2. Call StopMessageLoop() to exit message processing\n3. Return 1 (true) to indicate success\n\nParameters:\n  nUnused (Stack+0x4): Unused parameter, passed by callback mechanism\n\nReturns:\n  int: Always returns 1 (success)\n\nUsage:\n  Assigned to _g_pfnSubPanelCallback when player character is unavailable\n  in SetInventoryPanelVisibility. When triggered, cancels the pending\n  sub-panel operation and stops the message loop.\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  4 - Sub-panel state indicating cancelled/closed\n  1 - Return value indicating callback handled successfully\n\nCallers (via function pointer):\n  SetInventoryPanelVisibility - assigns as callback for unavailable player\n  Multiple UI initialization functions reference this address",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.08",
      "method": "API",
      "index": "API:b47aa581b88f98de842138279ab83621",
