      "name": "ResetInventorySubChildren",
      "signature": "void ResetInventorySubChildren(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "ResetInventorySubChildren - Cleanup function that resets inventory sub-panel state\n\nClassification: Cleanup/Destructor - Tears down sub-children state and restores input\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize loop counter to 0\n2. If g_nNumSubChildren > 0, iterate through g_apSubChildrenArray\n3. For each sub-child, call DispatchInventoryItemHandler to process/cleanup\n4. Increment counter and pointer, loop while counter < g_nNumSubChildren\n5. Reset g_nNumSubChildren to 0 (clear count)\n6. Call SetCurrentInputItem with g_dwCurrentInputItem to restore input state\n7. Reset g_dwInventorySubState to 0 (clear sub-state)\n\nParameters: None (void function)\n\nReturns: void\n\nGlobals Accessed:\n  g_nNumSubChildren (0x6fa21734) - Count of active sub-children, reset to 0\n  g_apSubChildrenArray (0x6fa20a20) - Array of sub-child descriptors\n  g_dwCurrentInputItem (0x6fa216d0) - Saved input item to restore\n  g_dwInventorySubState (0x6fa2173c) - Sub-panel state, reset to 0\n\nCallers: Called from 4 locations during UI state transitions",
