      "name": "ResetInventoryPanelToInitialState",
      "signature": "int ResetInventoryPanelToInitialState(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Resets the inventory panel UI to its initial state, clearing all slots and handlers.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call FUN_6fa10090 and FUN_6fa0f490 for panel pre-reset cleanup\n2. Dispatch inventory item handlers for slots 1-8 (addresses 0x6fa21818-0x6fa21838)\n3. Set current input item and pointer from global state\n4. Loop through sub-children array (g_apSubChildrenArray), dispatching handlers for each\n5. Reset g_nNumSubChildren to 0, call SetCurrentInputItem again\n6. Clear g_dwInventorySubState to 0\n7. Call FUN_6fa117b0 for additional state reset\n8. Clear g_dwInventoryExtraState, dispatch handlers for slots 9-10\n9. If g_dwSpecialModeFlag == 1, call FUN_6fa127f0\n10. If g_dwInventoryPanelMode == 3, reset it to 0\n11. If g_pInventoryPanelState is non-null, set bit mask with value 1\n12. Clear 9 panel state slots (g_dwPanelResetFlag through g_dwPanelStateSlot8)\n13. Set g_szCommandBufferEnd to 1000 (0x3E8)\n14. Check game list data byte at offset 0x225 and Ordinal_10002 result\n15. If conditions met: show string 0x1413, reset panel, clear buttons, create text box, return 1\n16. Otherwise: assert max children (0x20), create objects via factory, setup UI elements\n17. Return 1 on success\n\nParameters:\n  None (uses global state)\n\nReturns:\n  int - Always returns 1 (success)\n\nSSA Temporaries (compiler-generated, cannot be renamed):\n  piVar1: int * - pointer to created object from CreateObjectByTypeFactory\n  iVar2: int - loop counter for sub-children iteration, also holds Ordinal_10002 result\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- If sub-children count exceeds 0x1F (31), triggers FogAssert with file/line info\n- Special mode flag (0x6fa3e9cc) triggers additional processing via FUN_6fa127f0\n- Panel mode 3 is special case that gets reset to 0\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x1413: String ID for special mode text\n- 0x14C6: String ID for normal mode text\n- 0x1086: Assert line number for max children check\n- 0x20 (32): Maximum allowed sub-children count\n- 0x3E8 (1000): Command buffer end value\n- 0xFFFFFFFE (-2): Panel scroll offset reset value\n- 0x23: Panel display mode value\n- 0x10: Panel state decrement value\n\nOrdinal Calls:\n- Ordinal_10002: Checks special condition (returns 0 for special path)\n- Ordinal_10012: Called during normal panel setup to finalize display",
