      "name": "FinalizeFilteredGameListDisplay",
      "signature": "void FinalizeFilteredGameListDisplay(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Refreshes the game list UI control with filtered game entries and restores selection.\n\nWorker function called after filtering game list. Copies game entries from source\narray to display array, populates UI control with game names and player counts,\nthen attempts to restore previously selected game by name matching.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Early exit if g_pTextControl is NULL\n2. Save currently selected game name (Unicode to ANSI conversion) if any\n3. Get current selection index from text control\n4. Clear both primary and secondary text data lists\n5. Copy g_nGameListCount to g_nFilteredGameCount\n6. If no games, exit\n7. Check if player count display is enabled (Ordinal_10002)\n8. Copy game entries: memcpy source to dest (stride 0x3B = 59 bytes per entry)\n   - DWORD copy loop (uVar6 >> 2 iterations)\n   - Byte copy loop for remainder (uVar6 & 3 bytes)\n9. For each game entry (0 to g_nFilteredGameCount):\n   a. Add game name to text control (offset -0x30 from player count = name field)\n   b. If player count display enabled, convert count to string and append\n10. If previously selected game exists:\n    - Search for matching name using strcmp-style comparison\n    - Entry names start at g_aGameListEntriesDest + 1 (offset into entry)\n    - On match, call SetTextFieldValue to select that index\n11. Otherwise set selection index to 0\n12. Scroll to selected index\n\nParameters:\n  None (uses global state)\n\nReturns:\n  void\n\nGlobals Accessed:\n  g_pTextControl (0x6fa3e8c0) - Main text list control\n  g_pGameListSecondaryControl (0x6fa3e8c4) - Secondary list control\n  g_nGameListCount (0x6fa3e9d8) - Source game count\n  g_nFilteredGameCount (0x6fa3e9d4) - Filtered count (written)\n  g_aGameListEntriesSource (0x6fa30140) - Source game entry array\n  g_aGameListEntriesDest (0x6fa21ac8) - Destination entry array\n\nStructure Layout (Game Entry, 59 bytes / 0x3B):\n  Offset  Size  Field        Description\n  0x00    1     unknown      Entry type or flags\n  0x01    47    szGameName   Game name (ANSI string)\n  0x30    1     unknown      Padding or delimiter\n  0x31    2     wPlayerCount Player count (ushort at offset 0x31)\n  ...     ...   ...          Remaining fields\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - If no games in list, clears UI and exits early\n  - If no previous selection, defaults to index 0\n  - String comparison is case-sensitive, byte-by-byte\n\nCalled By:\n  FetchAndFilterGameListByDifficulty (0x6fa0e838)\n  FUN_6fa03249, FUN_6fa0327a",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.08",
