      "name": "ValidateGameNameCharacter",
      "signature": "bool ValidateGameNameCharacter(int nUnused1, int nUnused2, char * lpszChar)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "bool",
      "comment": "Validates a character for game name input fields.\n\nWARNING: Function boundaries are incomplete in Ghidra analysis. Only the first\ninstruction (MOV ECX, [g_pTextControl]) is included in the function body.\nThe actual function extends from 0x6fa0ef50 to 0x6fa0efb4 (100 bytes).\n\nAlgorithm (from manual disassembly):\n1. Load g_pTextControl global into ECX\n2. Set EDX = -1 (sentinel value)\n3. Call helper function (0x6fa129c6)\n4. Get character from lpszChar parameter [ESP+0x0C]\n5. Subtract 0x20 (space character) to normalize range\n6. If (char - 0x20) > 0x3F, go to secondary validation\n7. Use jump table lookup at 0x6fa0efb4 for character class\n8. Secondary validation checks:\n   - If char is '0'-'9' (0x30-0x39): return TRUE\n   - If char is 'a'-'z' (0x61-0x7a): return TRUE\n   - Otherwise: return FALSE\n\nParameters:\n  nUnused1 (int) - Unused parameter (stack cleanup)\n  nUnused2 (int) - Unused parameter (stack cleanup)\n  lpszChar (char *) - Pointer to character to validate\n\nReturns:\n  bool - TRUE (1) if character is valid for game name, FALSE (0) otherwise\n\nValid Characters:\n  - ASCII printable range 0x20-0x5F via lookup table\n  - Digits '0'-'9'\n  - Lowercase letters 'a'-'z'\n\nLookup Table at 0x6fa0efbc (64 bytes):\n  Maps characters 0x20-0x5F to valid (01) or invalid (00)\n  Pattern: 00 01 01 01 01 01 01 00 01 01 01 01 01 00 ...\n  Space (0x20) = invalid, most punctuation = valid\n\nJump Table at 0x6fa0efb4:\n  0x6fa0efa6 - Handle lowercase letter range\n  0x6fa0ef7e - Handle primary table lookup\n\nCalled By:\n  FinalizeFilteredGameListDisplay via MOV EDX, 0x6fa0ef50 at 0x6fa0eb86\n  Used as callback for edit box character validation\n\nCalling Convention: __stdcall (RET 0xC = 12 bytes, 3 DWORD params)",
