      "name": "HandleCreateGameButtonClick",
      "signature": "bool HandleCreateGameButtonClick(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "bool",
      "comment": "Handles Create Game button click in Battle.net/LAN multiplayer UI.\n\nClassification: Public API / UI Event Handler\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate MOTD OK button is active via GetUnitBitMask\n2. Get game name from g_pBnetGameNameLabel edit box\n3. Convert Unicode game name to Win ANSI (max 255 chars)\n4. Validate game name is not empty (strlen check)\n5. Get password from g_pBnetPasswordLabel edit box\n6. Get difficulty from g_pBnetDifficultyLabel edit box\n7. Check if Battle.net mode via Ordinal_10002 (D2Multi.IsBnetMode)\n8. If Battle.net mode:\n   a. Get max players from g_pBnetMaxPlayersLabel\n   b. Set uStack_304 = 1 (game creation flag)\n   c. Check max players toggle button validity\n   d. Parse max players input or use 0xFF default\n   e. Parse level restriction input\n9. Convert game name, password, difficulty to title case (16, 16, 32 chars)\n10. Build game flags: clear bits 12-14, OR in difficulty level shifted by 12\n11. Validate title-cased game name is not empty\n12. Branch based on game mode:\n    LAN Mode (Ordinal_10002 == 0):\n    - Read game flags at g_pGameListData+0x1EA\n    - Set expansion flag 0x800 if (flags & 4)\n    - Set hardcore flag 0x100000 if (flags & 0x20)\n    - Build difficulty char: (expansion?3:0) + diffLevel + '1'\n    - Copy difficulty string, call vtable callback at +0x34\n    - Show creating game message (string ID 0x147B)\n    - Run message pump with CheckVtableAndStopMessageLoop\n    - Call vtable callback at +0x98\n    - If game creation failed, show error (string ID 0x1412)\n    \n    Battle.net Mode:\n    - Save MAX_PLAYER to registry\n    - Save DIFF_LEVEL to registry\n    - Check toggle button, save LVL_REST (default 0x29A if disabled)\n13. Get local IP address\n14. Initialize game join with session data\n15. For Battle.net: reset error state, show message, run MCP pump\n16. On MCP error, shutdown MCP client\n17. Reset UI elements and reinitialize MOTD panel if needed\n\nParameters: None (uses global UI control pointers)\n\nReturns:\n  true (1) - Game creation initiated or completed\n  false (0) - Validation failed (MOTD not ready, empty game name)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Empty game name after conversion returns false immediately\n- LAN mode uses different message flow than Battle.net\n- Max players defaults to 0xFF if toggle disabled\n- Level restriction defaults to 0x29A (666) if toggle disabled\n\nRegistry Keys Written (Battle.net only):\n- HKCU\\Software\\Blizzard Entertainment\\Diablo II\\MAX_PLAYER\n- HKCU\\Software\\Blizzard Entertainment\\Diablo II\\DIFF_LEVEL\n- HKCU\\Software\\Blizzard Entertainment\\Diablo II\\LVL_REST\n\nFlag Bits at g_pGameListData+0x1EA:\n- 0x04: Expansion mode flag\n- 0x20: Hardcore mode flag\n\nFlag Bits at g_pGameListData+0x204:\n- 0x0800: Expansion game flag\n- 0x100000: Hardcore game flag\n\nString IDs:\n- 0x147B: \"Creating game...\" message\n- 0x1412: Game creation error message\n\nOrdinal References:\n- Ordinal_10002: D2Multi.IsBnetMode - Returns non-zero if Battle.net\n- Ordinal_10052: D2Multi.IsMcpConnected - Returns non-zero if MCP connected",
