      "name": "InitializeGameListPanelMode",
      "signature": "int InitializeGameListPanelMode(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Initializes the game list panel mode for multiplayer UI.\n\nClassification: Initialization function - Sets up panel state for game list display.\n\nNOTE: Function boundary only includes first CALL instruction (0x6fa11030).\nRemaining code at 0x6fa11035-0x6fa1107f is orphaned but decompiler inlines it.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Reset inventory panel state to clean slate (call ResetInventoryPanelState)\n2. Set g_dwInventoryPanelMode = 3 (game list mode identifier)\n3. Initialize game list panel controls (call InitializeGameListPanel)\n4. Clear button frame values for three UI button objects:\n   - g_apBnetUIObjects[7] - Button cleared to frame 0\n   - g_apBnetUIObjects[6] - Button cleared to frame 0  \n   - g_apBnetUIObjects[9] - Button cleared to frame 0\n5. Return 1 (success)\n\nParameters: None\n\nReturns: int - Always returns 1 (success)\n\nCallers: Referenced from data at 0x6fa1b2f0 (likely function pointer table)\n\nGlobals Modified:\n- g_dwInventoryPanelMode: Set to 3 (game list panel mode)\n\nSide Effects:\n- Resets inventory panel state via ResetInventoryPanelState\n- Initializes game list panel via InitializeGameListPanel\n- Clears button states for UI objects 6, 7, and 9",
